Disable the in-app updater. It polls the GitHub release feed and nags, but an
unpacked install (not an AppImage) can never be updated by it: Portage does.

From the PF4Public overlay (dev-util/orca/files/disable-in-app-auto-update.patch).
--- a/src/main/updater/lifecycle/updater-setup.ts
+++ b/src/main/updater/lifecycle/updater-setup.ts
@@ -170,9 +170,13 @@
       this.sendErrorStatus(`The server update did not complete: ${serveHandoffFailure}`, true)
     }
 
-    if (!app.isPackaged) {
-      return
-    }
+    // Gentoo: the in-app auto-updater is disabled. Orca is installed and
+    // upgraded via portage, and on an unpacked (non-AppImage) install the
+    // updater classifies the package type as "unusable" — it can only poll
+    // the GitHub release feed and nag, never install. Return unconditionally
+    // (the same state as !app.isPackaged / dev) so no feed URL is set and no
+    // background check, resume/focus check, or update nudge is scheduled.
+    return
 
     const autoUpdater = this.getAutoUpdater()
     configureMacShipItScheduling()
